[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit"]
[Variation "King's Gambit Declined: Classical Defence"]
[ECO "C30"]
[Character "solid,sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "both"]
[Tricks "trap"]
[Themes "bishop-c5,centre-pawns"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Opponent "2.f4"]
[Start "1. e4 e5"]

2. f4 { The King's Gambit. White offers the f-pawn so that Black's e-pawn leaves the centre, then White takes the centre with d4 and gets the open f-file. } 2... Bc5 { Declines the pawn and develops. The bishop eyes f2 and sets a trap: if White takes on e5, ...Qh4+ wins at once. } 3. Nf3 { Guards h4 so ...Qh4+ is no threat, and attacks e5. Do not take on e5 yet. } 3... d6 { Protects e5 and opens the bishop on c8. } 4. c3 { Prepares d4 to take the whole centre. The pawn on c3 also gives the queen's knight the d2 square. } ( 4. Bc4 Nf6 5. d3 Nc6 ) ( 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. Bc4 Nc6 ) 4... Nf6 { Attacks e4 and develops. If White plays d4, Black takes and the bishop steps back to b6. } 5. d4 ( 5. fxe5 dxe5 6. Nxe5 Qe7 7. d4 Bd6 ) 5... exd4 6. cxd4 Bb6 { Keeps the bishop on the diagonal aimed at d4 and out of reach of any pawn push. } 7. Nc3 O-O { The king is safe and the rook joins the game. } 8. Bd3 ( 8. e5 Ng4 9. h3 Nh6 ) 8... Nc6 { Adds a second attacker to d4, which White must keep guarding. } 9. Bc2 Re8 { The rook eyes e4, which White has to keep guarded. } 10. O-O Bg4 { Pins the knight on f3 to the queen, so d4 loses a guard. Black's plan: keep piling up on d4 and use the rook on e8 against e4. } *
